 "description": "<div><span style='font-size:medium;'>The Esri Canada Light Grey Community Map of Canada is designed to be used as a basemap by GIS professionals and as a reference map by anyone.&nbsp;This layer is used to create the Light Grey style.&nbsp;The map includes city boundaries, cities, water features, parks, landmarks, transportation, buildings, parcels and address points and can be overlaid on a shaded relief for context.</span></div><div><br />&nbsp;</div><div><span style='font-size:medium;'><span>The map is compiled from a variety of authoritative sources including Natural Resources Canada, the Provinces and Territories and Canadian municipalities</span></span></div><div><br />&nbsp;</div><p><span style='font-size:medium;'><span>If you see a problem in the Community Map of Canada that you would like to report, please use the </span></span><a target='_blank' href='https://survey123.arcgis.com/share/03e20f4c996d41b5b5a92eecbca99bb3?webMapId=98652eb8458a464fa95feb9bd812b29a' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:medium;'><span>Community Map of Canada Feedback App</span></span></a><span style='font-size:medium;'><span>. This feedback will be reviewed by the Esri Canada Community Maps team and considered for inclusion in our updates.</span></span></p><p><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>You can add this layer to the ArcGIS Online Map Viewer and ArcGIS Pro. To view this layer in a web map, see this&nbsp;</span><a target='_blank' href='https://exchange.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=e1de1cfd7a624639b65e2cc0f10aad70' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Light Grey / Nuances de gris (pâle)</a><span style='font-family:Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>&nbsp;basemap.</span><br />&nbsp;</p>",
